<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian company profits jump in Dec qtr.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian company profits jump in Dec qtr.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pre-tax profits of Australian companies with more than 30 employees rose 8.6 percent in the December quarter to A$12.024 billion from A$11.071 billion (revised from A$10.536 billion) in the September quarter, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>This compares with a revised A$10.940 billion a year earlier.</p>
<p>Figures are seasonally-adjusted and are also before interest and depreciation.</p>
<p>The bureau said it had revised up profit figures back to December 1994.  </p>
<p>Company profits before income tax, net interest paid and depreciation --	    (All figures in A$ million)</p>
<p>				 Dec qtr 96 Sept qtr 96  Dec qtr 95</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted    12,024     11,071     10,940</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		 13,141     11,775     12,004</p>
<p>    Trend Estimates	  11,578     11,337     11,287</p>
<p>(Seasonally-adjusted, profits before income tax)</p>
<p>    Mining			1,821	1,481	1,514</p>
<p>    Manufacturing	     2,619	2,356	2,868</p>
<p>    Construction		  109	  130	   93</p>
</text>
